>
>The big win for Monks is the crossbow bolt at WGT 1 

  Requires finding, carrying and wielding a non-cursed crossbow 
of weight 50.  50 units of weight that is useless as a direct 
weapon.  When bashing its main effect is to break "never hit with 
a wielded weapon" conduct.

  Crossbow bolts also don't get the strength damage bonus, since 
they're fired from a launcher.  Knives, daggers, rocks, gems, glass,
shuriken, etc. do get the strength bonus.  

  (Note: Crossbow bolts thrown without wielding a crossbow get a -4 
to hit bonus.)

  The damage is better, but not nearly enough to make up for the 
finicky, tedious finding, wielding, unwielding, using, care, 
replenishment, deadweight, and maintenance. 

  Non-multishot isn't worth that.

  Another problem with launcher based weapons is when to switch to 
wielded weapon for fighting at melee range.  With multi-shot launcher, 
like Expert Elven Ranger firing d5 highly enchanted Elven arrows from 
an Elven bow this isn't a problem.  

  With unskilled or basic skilled monk firing a single crossbow bolt,
it is a problem.

  For no-hands missile weapons like daggers, darts, knives, shuriken,
rocks, glass, etc it's also not a problem.  You can use them and
still wield whatever melee weapon you like, or no weapon at all
for martial arts combat.

>and better average 
>damage than ordinary knives or daggers, but silver damage and no 
>automatic reloads from traps.


  Difficult to find/replenish, they vanish if not blessed and 
with high luck, and require a launcher be wielded.  Wielding 
a launcher is tedious and easy to forget.  Forgetting makes 
the missile much less effective.  Forgetting to unwield can 
break "never hit with a wielded weapon" conduct.


  I'll bet almost no one has ever #enhanced a monk to basic in
crossbow.  Even fewer have ever enchanted a crossbow bolt,
much less a crossbow.  Anyone?


  Worthless glass is better.  Since almost all early gems are likely
to be worthless glass, they're nearly ideal as first missile weapons for 
all roles and races.  

  Rocks are a special case since you can usually get some if 
you need them. 

  Spear or javelin would also be better: no hands, strength bonus,
don't vanish, can be used wielded.  If used wielded a silver spear
can be wished for guaranteed.  Wielding also makes maximum use of 
skill slots.  They also get a to-hit bonus when thrown.

  Darts would be better, since they don't require wielding/carrying
a heavy launcher and are much more easily obtained.

  Boomerangs are better because they have a +4 to-hit bonus, do 5 base
damage, return, are no-hands, get the strength damage bonus, and can 
hit off center.

